  [1mTask[0m — [38;5;153m{ id, title, done, dueAt, createdAt }[39m, where [38;5;153mdueAt[39m is epoch ms or [38;5;153mnull[39m. Tasks without a due date simply never
  produce reminders, which keeps "no reminder" a data state rather than a special case.

  [1mStorage[0m — [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m, two independent keys, each with a [38;5;153mversion[39m field so a later shape change has somewhere to hang
  a migration:
  - [38;5;153mtasks.v1[39m → [38;5;153m{ version: 1, tasks: [...] }[39m
  - [38;5;153mnotifications.dismissed.v1[39m → [38;5;153m{ version: 1, keys: [...] }[39m

  Separate keys so clearing notification state never risks the tasks.

  [1mReminder[0m (computed, never stored) — [38;5;153m{ key, taskId, title, level, dueAt }[39m where [38;5;153mlevel[39m is [38;5;153m'soon' | 'overdue'[39m.

  [1m[38;5;153mdueReminders(tasks, now, dismissed)[39m:[0m
  - skip tasks that are [38;5;153mdone[39m or have [38;5;153mdueAt === null[39m
  - [38;5;153moverdue[39m when [38;5;153mnow >= dueAt[39m; [38;5;153msoon[39m when [38;5;153mdueAt - now <= 60 min[39m and not yet due
  - a task yields [1mat most one[0m reminder — [38;5;153moverdue[39m supersedes [38;5;153msoon[39m
  - drop anything whose key is in [38;5;153mdismissed[39m; sort by [38;5;153mdueAt[39m ascending

  [1mTwo details worth your attention, because they're judgment calls:[0m

  [3mDismissal key includes the due date:[0m [38;5;153m${taskId}:${dueAt}:${level}[39m. Push a task's deadline back and its reminders re-arm
  automatically — a dismissal applies to [3mthat[0m deadline, not to the task forever. This is what makes "derived,
  stateless" actually work; without the [38;5;153mdueAt[39m in the key you'd need explicit reset-on-edit logic.

  [3mDismissing "soon" does not dismiss "overdue":[0m they're distinct keys, so waving off "due in an hour" still lets the
  task shout when it's actually late. I think that's right — silencing a warning shouldn't silence the alarm — but it's
  the kind of thing that annoys people if they disagree with it, so say the word if you want one dismissal to cover
  both.

  [1m60 minutes[0m for the "soon" window is a guess. It's a single exported constant, trivial to change, and I'd rather not
  build a settings UI for it unless you want one.

  Does this hold up, or do you want the dismissal or window behaviour different?

